From 285c614928367763e036142e3600f2a3909bbf7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:35:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] win32: declare -monitorHandleForScreen: in
 WIN32Server.h

-resolutionForScreen: calls it, ahead of its definition in
WIN32Server.m, to find a monitor's DPI.  GCC, without a declaration,
took it to return id and warned that the argument to monitorDPI() was
of an incompatible type; clang didn't warn.  Found building with MinGW
GCC and GCC's runtime, as GNUstep's patch policy asks.

AI assistance: this change and its description were written with Claude
(Anthropic's Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Headers/win32/WIN32Server.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Headers/win32/WIN32Server.h b/Headers/win32/WIN32Server.h
index efda610..0aaef87 100644
--- a/Headers/win32/WIN32Server.h
+++ b/Headers/win32/WIN32Server.h
@@ -140,6 +140,9 @@ typedef struct w32serverFlags
  */
 - (BOOL) isPerMonitorDPIAware;
 
+/** The Windows monitor showing screen, or NULL. */
+- (HMONITOR) monitorHandleForScreen: (int)screen;
+
 /** Declares the parts of a window's caption row the gui drew, for a
  * window whose client draws its caption.  Each rect, in the window's base
  * coordinates, has a kind from GSCaptionRegionKind: the parts that drag
